{"id": "q0422", "pool": "easy-chat", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The earliest ancestors of Native Americans were groups of people who migrated to the Americas from Asia across a land bridge called B erosia Strait. These early people are believed to have arrived around 15,00 0 years ago during the last ice age. They gradually spread throughout North and South America, adapt ing to diverse environments over thousands of years.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
